# Paths a person reviews, whatever the reviewer concludes (ADR-0048).
#
# The "Pull requests are reviewed" ruleset requires a code owner's approval, so an approval
# from the reviewing app satisfies it only for a pull request touching none of these. That is
# the boundary, and GitHub enforces it — not the reviewer, and not scripts/review_policy.py,
# which reads this file so the list exists once.
#
# Only three pattern forms, because the policy script refuses any other: an anchored
# directory (/infra/), an anchored file (/REVIEW.md), a bare name at any depth (CLAUDE.md).

# CI, this file, the dependency schedule, the review workflow — and the gates and the policy
# themselves. A change that weakens CI is a blocker, so it is never self-approved.
/.github/                 @geoffscott
/scripts/                 @geoffscott
/REVIEW.md                @geoffscott

# Booking semantics, the write path, authentication and the schema migrations all live in
# the ledger, and CLAUDE.md puts each behind human review.
/src/cfokit/ledger/       @geoffscott

# Infrastructure and the environment contract (ADR-0016).
/infra/                   @geoffscott

# The constitution: the rules, the records that hold their reasoning, and what they derive from.
CLAUDE.md                 @geoffscott
/docs/decisions/          @geoffscott
/docs/product/            @geoffscott

# The published interfaces. A diff here is a contract change (ADR-0015).
/docs/contracts/          @geoffscott
